.Dd October 31, 2026
.Dt SQLITE3 1
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm sqlite3
.Nd command-line interface to SQLite databases
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar database
.Op Ar sql
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
opens the SQLite database file
.Ar database ,
or a temporary in-memory one, and runs the SQL statements given as
.Ar sql
or read from standard input. Lines starting with a dot are the shell's
own commands:
.Ql .tables ,
.Ql .schema ,
.Ql .mode ,
.Ql .import ,
.Ql .dump ,
.Ql .help
lists them all.
.Pp
Among the options:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl csv , Fl json , Fl line , Fl list , Fl column , Fl box
The output mode.
.It Fl header , Fl noheader
Column names first, or not.
.It Fl cmd Ar command
Run
.Ar command
before reading the input.
.It Fl readonly
Open the database read only.
.It Fl version
Print SQLite's version.
.It Fl help
List every option.
.El
.Pp
The library is
.Pa /usr/lib/libsqlite3.dylib ,
with full-text search (FTS3, FTS4, FTS5), R-Tree and JSON.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl sqlite3 data.db "select count(*) from items;"
.Dl echo "create table t(x); insert into t values(1);" | sqlite3 data.db
.Sh SEE ALSO
The SQL language and the shell are documented at
.Lk https://www.sqlite.org/docs.html .
